  "data_vs_prose": "The data shows a commodity endpoint-engine release: 10 ClamAV High/7.5 automatable defects with mid-band EPSS and no exploitation, against 6 CVEs with EPSS \u226550% that carry no severity metadata at all. The prose shows the opposite emphasis and worse hygiene: the newsroom's highest-volume coverage is four Intersight CVEs published under the CVE-2026-123007 NGINX headline, so 6/5/3/3/3 article counts measure headline reuse, not independent reporting on those four IDs. Three ClamAV CVEs are filed under 'Java2Shell', which mislabels a C-vs-Java stack. Only the NGINX integer-underflow-to-RCE characterisation, and the 'native code' framing, come from prose and cannot be derived from the data \u2014 the data has no CVSS and no description beyond internal labels. Two things the data does assert and the prose ignores: the ISE family contributes 5 CVEs with no corresponding row, CVE or article anywhere in this view, and with_kb 0 is a Microsoft-template field surviving into a Cisco release, not evidence of missing patches.",
