  "patch_note": "Intersight Virtual Appliance first \u2014 five CVEs at EPSS 0.97\u20130.98 on an internet-facing management plane, and the only items here that look like remote code execution. Second, the OpenJDK/Java4Shell surface (CVE-2026-114938): inventory which Cisco products bundle the affected JDK rather than assuming the family is small. Third, Secure Endpoint: ship the ClamAV engine/content update that covers the ten engine CVEs, prioritising the OLE2 and XAR size/scan-time bypasses over the pure DoS bugs, and verify the engine build actually advanced rather than only the management console. Cisco ISE: five CVEs are attributed to the family but appear nowhere in the scored set or the coverage list \u2014 confirm whether they exist, which IDs they are, and that the fix is applied before closing the release. Nothing here is KEV-listed or observed exploited, so no emergency change window is justified beyond Intersight.",
